KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp23
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ pack expansion in a subscript: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
The expression-list of a subscript may contain a pack expansion
([expr.sub]/1, [temp.variadic]/5): `m[a...]' was a parse error
(cpp23_subscript_pack_expansion_forms).  libstdc++ 16's <utility>
(std::constant_wrapper::operator[]) uses this in C++26 mode.
